# MAP.md, BACKLOG_OPEN.md and docs/UI-INVENTORY.md are GENERATED (scripts/build-map.mjs, build-backlog-index.mjs,
# ui-audit/ui-inventory.mjs) and a branch never touches them (scripts/generated-doc-touch-guard.mjs; the nightly
# .github/workflows/regen-derived-docs.yml refreshes them). They get git's own zero-config `union` driver so that a local merge
# of a branch that predates that rule never shows a conflict marker: whatever union leaves is corrected the next time the generator
# runs. No custom merge driver, hook or `npm install` step is involved (the old planyr-ledger driver was retired with the ledger
# move onto its own branch, 2026-11-05 — see CLAUDE.md "THE LEDGER LIVES ON ITS OWN GIT BRANCH"). test/freshCloneMerge.test.js
# proves these lines work in a bare clone.
MAP.md merge=union
BACKLOG_OPEN.md merge=union
docs/UI-INVENTORY.md merge=union
